            <ArticleTitle>Primary tuberculosis of stomach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>187-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastric tuberculosis is mostly secondary to pulmonary tuberculosis. Primary and isolated gastric tuberculosis is very rare. A case of primary gastric tuberculosis of stomach in a 45-year-old female, known diabetic and hypertensive who presented to the hospital with epigastric pain and vomiting is being reported. Endoscopy showed a gastric ulcerated nodular lesion and biopsy showed tuberculous granuloma. Repeat endoscopy after a course of antituberculosis treatment showed minimal gastritis and complete resolution of the ulcerated nodular lesion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
